I didn't sign him up so he could win some ribbon like it was a dog show.

00:27:51.210 --> 00:27:56.220
Wanting him to hear some live musicians and see that jazz is a living heart.

00:27:57.350 --> 00:27:58.650
He's a little too much in his head.

00:28:05.240 --> 00:28:06.400
What is this piece? Do you know?

00:28:07.960 --> 00:28:09.760
If I want enough, I'm going deaf. Just ask.

00:28:12.700 --> 00:28:13.780
How long has it been going on?

00:28:14.140 --> 00:28:16.690
Since the explosion. It's been getting worse.

00:28:17.580 --> 00:28:19.800
Doctor says something about damaged hair cells.

00:28:19.900 --> 00:28:21.660
They're doing some amazing things with implants.

00:28:22.880 --> 00:28:25.640
And there are new drugs that could really help with the sensorineural damage.

00:28:25.800 --> 00:28:28.660
No, I've heard that pitch before. I'm not interested.

00:28:31.460 --> 00:28:32.480
Why not at least try?

00:28:32.640 --> 00:28:33.280
That's all I'm saying.

00:28:33.600 --> 00:28:35.940
When you get to be my age, you're bound to do something.

00:28:36.080 --> 00:28:39.300
My eyes are so good, as long as you know what you're seeing,

00:28:40.510 --> 00:28:42.170
even watching the great ones is a thrill.

00:28:43.380 --> 00:28:44.160
Watch your son.

00:28:45.300 --> 00:28:46.120
He could be next.

00:28:48.280 --> 00:28:50.100
I may not be the best teacher for him anymore.

00:28:51.570 --> 00:28:53.800
You know it, and I know it.

00:29:10.970 --> 00:29:14.400
Delia, I know you're mad at me, but I'd like to talk to you, if that's okay.

00:29:27.660 --> 00:29:29.890
You know, um, when I was in, uh...

00:29:30.350 --> 00:29:36.640
Bangladesh once. I was in this mud hut and there was a hole on the roof and we had to fix it and

00:29:36.640 --> 00:29:42.000
all I had was a rope and no ladder and then it started to rain and I had to go out and cut

00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:51.440
down a bunch of palm leaves and I forgot why I started telling you this story. It's okay.

00:29:52.090 --> 00:29:59.890
It's kind of boring anyway. Delia, I'm sorry about the diary.

00:30:01.470 --> 00:30:03.090
You're right. I shouldn't have worked on it.

00:30:03.150 --> 00:30:05.130
I probably didn't even do a very good job anyway.

00:30:06.820 --> 00:30:08.040
You looked pretty good.

00:30:08.220 --> 00:30:08.660
You think?

00:30:10.180 --> 00:30:12.720
Still, though, terrible idea on my part.

00:30:20.980 --> 00:30:23.560
Never knew how hard it was to take care of a 10-year-old.

00:30:26.340 --> 00:30:27.680
Don't have to take care of me.

00:30:28.420 --> 00:30:28.900
I know.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:41.550
wanted to help your dad out so he could spend the weekend with Ephraim. Honestly, I was hoping that if

00:30:41.550 --> 00:30:46.870
you and I had some more time alone together you might like me more. I know it doesn't seem like it

00:30:46.870 --> 00:30:51.240
but I really was trying to do the right thing. I guess I'm just, I'm pretty terrible at this

00:30:51.240 --> 00:30:59.370
parenting thing. Pretty much. But you're trying. And in school we also get grades for Ephraim.

00:31:10.840 --> 00:31:11.840
Thank you, Shauna Yawke.

00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:15.700
Our next performer is a pianist from Everwood, Colorado,

00:31:16.900 --> 00:31:18.340
studying under Willingham, Cleveland.

00:31:18.970 --> 00:31:20.590
Please welcome Ephraim Brown.

00:32:03.100 --> 00:32:03.280
Thank you.

00:32:41.070 --> 00:32:43.470
If I have one of those books on tape, maybe we could...

00:32:43.470 --> 00:32:43.630
No.

00:32:43.810 --> 00:32:48.930
It wasn't that big a deal, Ephraim,

00:32:48.990 --> 00:32:50.850
just a little performance anxiety, that's all.

00:32:50.950 --> 00:32:51.790
It happens to the best of me.

00:32:52.390 --> 00:32:54.230
You know, when I first performed surgery,

00:32:54.270 --> 00:32:56.030
I was so nervous that I dropped a scalpel.

00:32:56.700 --> 00:32:57.570
Stop, please.

00:32:57.790 --> 00:32:59.130
Just stop, I'm begging you.

00:33:00.160 --> 00:33:00.880
I'm just trying to help.

00:33:00.940 --> 00:33:02.960
Man, you can't and you won't, so just give it up.

00:33:03.650 --> 00:33:04.070
Pull over.

00:33:04.450 --> 00:33:04.710
What?

00:33:04.850 --> 00:33:05.630
Well, we're almost home.

00:33:05.750 --> 00:33:06.130
We can't wait.

00:33:06.290 --> 00:33:07.670
I said pull over.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:30.260
Just to see.

00:34:00.560 --> 00:34:03.130
Honey, are you OK?

00:34:03.970 --> 00:34:05.160
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:34:06.740 --> 00:34:07.940
Come on, let's check it out.

00:34:13.770 --> 00:34:16.310
As fascinating a study of Americana as this is,

00:34:16.310 --> 00:34:17.190
what are we doing here?

00:34:17.880 --> 00:34:18.740
Well, couldn't this wait?

00:34:18.940 --> 00:34:21.360
I mean, how badly could you need new socks?

00:34:21.600 --> 00:34:23.320
When they finally kick Bright out of Victoria's Secret,

00:34:23.420 --> 00:34:24.400
he's not going to be able to find us.

00:34:30.640 --> 00:34:30.880
Play.

00:34:31.420 --> 00:34:32.260
You're joking, right?

00:34:32.590 --> 00:34:34.490
What is this, a cable access version of punk?

00:34:34.960 --> 00:34:35.820
How long have you known me?

00:34:36.160 --> 00:34:36.500
I don't know.

00:34:36.640 --> 00:34:36.960
A while.

00:34:37.630 --> 00:34:39.150
How many jokes have I told?

00:34:40.070 --> 00:34:40.810
Now, go ahead and play.

00:34:41.830 --> 00:34:43.170
Look, I appreciate what you're trying to do,

00:34:43.250 --> 00:34:45.630
but I'm in no mood to do the get back up on the horse thing,

00:34:45.810 --> 00:34:45.990
all right?

00:34:46.150 --> 00:34:47.190
Whoever this girl is,

00:34:47.760 --> 00:34:48.980
she made you play your best,

00:34:49.650 --> 00:34:50.690
and she made you play your worst.

00:34:50.890 --> 00:34:51.190
Wait a minute.

00:34:51.250 --> 00:34:52.170
This is about a girl?

00:34:52.310 --> 00:34:53.730
It's always about a girl.

00:34:54.170 --> 00:34:56.510
Now, go ahead and get her out of your system.

00:34:56.880 --> 00:34:57.800
Well, I thought you weren't supposed to play

00:34:57.800 --> 00:34:58.660
for anybody but yourself.

00:34:59.180 --> 00:34:59.940
You think I was born?

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:09.630
old and alone. I've been there. Love and heartbreak, pleasure and pain. In the end, it's all passion,

00:35:10.910 --> 00:35:11.490
use and vote.

00:35:33.520 --> 00:35:33.780
Thank you.

00:36:02.300 --> 00:36:03.040
How did you know?

00:36:03.850 --> 00:36:06.700
Well, some people see the forest, some people see the trees.

00:36:08.390 --> 00:36:10.990
I don't know if you just insulted me or not, but it really doesn't matter.

00:36:12.230 --> 00:36:16.300
As long as you can make my son play like that, I can't think of a better teacher for you.

00:36:16.460 --> 00:36:20.980
You know what? I'm going to miss this.

00:36:35.500 --> 00:36:38.180
I didn't know food could cost this much. I mean, chicken is chicken, right?

00:36:38.420 --> 00:36:41.000
Yeah, and whatever truffles are, I hope there's, like, gold in them.

00:36:42.160 --> 00:36:43.300
We really don't need to eat here.

00:36:43.660 --> 00:36:46.480
No, no, it's fine. I picked up a couple extra shifts at the drugstore.

00:36:47.380 --> 00:36:50.420
The real drugstore, not the one I ran out of my trunk.

00:36:50.620 --> 00:36:56.460
I wanted this to be special, you know?

00:36:56.680 --> 00:36:59.940
Not that I don't enjoy our Whopper meals together, but, um...

00:37:00.060 --> 00:37:05.210
This is sort of a new start for me and for us.

00:37:05.350 --> 00:37:08.830
I wanted to thank you for giving me another chance.

00:37:10.750 --> 00:37:13.060
Show you how much better of a person you make me.

00:37:13.570 --> 00:37:15.050
You don't need me to be that person.

00:37:16.810 --> 00:37:21.250
I know. I don't want to be that person without you.

00:37:24.910 --> 00:37:26.010
I'm starving. What are you going to get?

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:32.510
I have no idea how to pronounce any of this.

00:37:33.320 --> 00:37:35.950
What's the French word for bathroom?

00:37:36.530 --> 00:37:37.490
I don't know, lejeune?

00:37:37.850 --> 00:37:38.330
Lejeune.

00:38:09.310 --> 00:38:12.230
Now we want us to play every weekend for the next couple of months.

00:38:12.390 --> 00:38:12.990
Isn't that incredible?

00:38:13.210 --> 00:38:13.750
That's great.

00:38:14.380 --> 00:38:17.080
Oh, and the owner said that he could probably get a couple of people to come out and listen

00:38:17.080 --> 00:38:20.020
to us because he has these unbelievable connections from when he lived in L.A.

00:38:20.730 --> 00:38:21.390
I'll be huge.

00:38:24.430 --> 00:38:24.770
Oh, my.

00:38:25.680 --> 00:38:28.140
I've been all about me since the minute you walked in the door.

00:38:28.260 --> 00:38:29.520
I haven't even asked about your concert.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:32.960
No, your story is way better. Trust me.

00:38:33.360 --> 00:38:34.600
How was it? You killed, didn't you?

00:38:35.170 --> 00:38:36.950
There was definitely some dying involved.

00:38:38.160 --> 00:38:39.380
I sort of didn't play.

00:38:41.630 --> 00:38:42.870
What happened? Did you get sick or something?

00:38:43.470 --> 00:38:48.230
No, it wasn't so much sick as it was the all-night drive from Boulder

00:38:48.510 --> 00:38:49.930
back to your house and back again.

00:38:50.130 --> 00:38:50.750
It kind of wrecked me.

00:38:52.790 --> 00:38:55.640
You drove back here when? Why?

00:38:57.150 --> 00:38:57.810
Forget it.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:01.080
I don't understand. Why did you come back here?

00:39:03.210 --> 00:39:13.150
Well, you know, I thought I figured that I probably really freaked you out with the whole I love you thing that, you know, you'd be obsessing about it, but you obviously weren't because I came back here and I saw you and you were fine.

00:39:14.840 --> 00:39:16.380
Wait, you saw me and you didn't come in?

00:39:16.460 --> 00:39:24.240
Well, I didn't want to be like the crazy person barging in, though I'm probably not helping my case too much by telling you all this.

00:39:27.440 --> 00:39:28.520
Oh, this is, um...

00:39:29.090 --> 00:39:29.930
Horrifying? I know.

00:39:31.560 --> 00:39:32.980
It's just a little crazy, Ephraim.

00:39:33.080 --> 00:39:34.660
That's what the voice in my head kept telling me

00:39:34.660 --> 00:39:35.700
the entire drive back to the hotel.

00:39:40.440 --> 00:39:41.340
I should have said something.

00:39:41.540 --> 00:39:43.800
When you said it, it just caught me off guard,

00:39:43.800 --> 00:39:48.290
and I didn't want to say anything, like, reflexively.

00:39:48.330 --> 00:39:50.730
If that's a word, I don't know what I'm saying right now.

00:39:50.850 --> 00:39:50.870
It's OK.

00:39:51.690 --> 00:39:52.010
It's all right.

00:39:54.350 --> 00:39:57.260
I wasn't planning on ignoring it, or you.

00:39:57.360 --> 00:39:59.910
I just didn't want to say anything.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:01.680
at first because I wanted to process it.

00:40:01.840 --> 00:40:03.480
I wanted to figure out how I felt.

00:40:03.700 --> 00:40:06.910
I never thought that you would drive all the way back here.

00:40:07.600 --> 00:40:08.220
It's fine.

00:40:09.710 --> 00:40:10.150
I'm worried about it.

00:40:10.990 --> 00:40:11.610
I am worried.

00:40:14.160 --> 00:40:16.900
Look, I was just excited about last weekend and everything.

00:40:17.040 --> 00:40:19.300
It's not like I'm psychotically in love with you or anything.

00:40:22.220 --> 00:40:25.220
Do you think we could just maybe rewind the last couple days,

00:40:25.400 --> 00:40:26.400
just go back completely?

00:40:26.620 --> 00:40:29.840
I don't think it works that way, Ephraim.

00:40:33.040 --> 00:40:36.420
Right, yeah, yeah, toothpaste, too, forgot.

00:40:42.380 --> 00:40:45.960
I think we could maybe just pretend now at least.

00:40:50.360 --> 00:40:51.380
Yeah, I guess we could do that.

00:41:03.580 --> 00:41:06.940
so you guys really had a good time absolutely and she brushed her teeth

00:41:06.940 --> 00:41:12.230
that's usually her favorite delay tactic that and needing another drink of water before she

00:41:12.230 --> 00:41:17.190
can sleep she kind of turns into a sponge right before bedtime no i told you everything was great

00:41:17.250 --> 00:41:22.060
wow you're gonna have to tell me your secret weapon i've never gotten through a weekend

00:41:22.060 --> 00:41:25.120
with that kind of success not without nina anyway

00:41:31.440 --> 00:41:36.200
You know what? Kids are a mystery, aren't they?

00:41:36.740 --> 00:41:38.720
Prop circles pale in comparison.

00:41:39.440 --> 00:41:41.800
It does get easier.

00:41:44.130 --> 00:41:47.190
Sweetie, Linda was just telling me what a great time you guys had this weekend.

00:41:47.670 --> 00:41:51.150
I think we should have Sundays and celebrate your dad's return.

00:41:51.390 --> 00:41:51.850
What do you say?

00:41:51.970 --> 00:41:52.590
Works for me.

00:41:52.730 --> 00:41:53.110
All right.

00:41:53.510 --> 00:41:56.200
Oh, I get your trick. Frozen sugar.

00:41:56.300 --> 00:41:58.940
Three hot fudge sundaes coming up with extra bananas.

00:42:01.280 --> 00:42:01.900
So what's that about?

00:42:02.670 --> 00:42:02.970
Nothing.

00:42:03.480 --> 00:42:04.480
Ah, secrets, huh?

00:42:06.860 --> 00:42:08.720
Yeah, it's a secret.

00:42:19.660 --> 00:42:25.160
Sometimes it's easier to pretend things are okay rather than face a difficult truth.

00:42:26.220 --> 00:42:29.980
So we go through the motions, the rituals of everyday life.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:37.760
life we hope the comfortable rhythms of familiarity will hold off the inevitable just a little longer

00:42:41.440 --> 00:42:59.020
return things to normal anything to buy us more time plain pretend make believe it might be the

00:42:59.020 --> 00:42:59.980
one thing we never

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:00.580
outgrow.
